  "title": "Activation Energy",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The minimum energy necessary to form a product during a collision between reactants is called the "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "activation energy ("
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "E"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ")"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The minimum energy molecules need to react; the height of the energy barrier to formation of products."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "3162319791",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2166483903",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": ". The "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "kinetic energy"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Energy of a moving body, in joules, equal to 1/2 "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "mv"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " (where "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "m"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " = mass and "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "v"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " = velocity). "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "1839667515",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "304233652",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " of reactant molecules has an important role in a reaction because the energy needed to form a product is provided by a collision of a reactant molecule with another reactant molecule. (In single-reactant reactions, activation energy may be provided by a collision of the reactant molecule with the wall of the reaction vessel or with molecules of an inert contaminant.) If the activation energy is much larger than the average kinetic energy of the molecules, only a few fast-moving molecules will have enough energy to react, so the reaction will occur slowly. If the activation energy is much smaller than the average kinetic energy of the molecules, a large fraction of the molecules will possess the necessary kinetic energy. Most collisions between molecules will therefore result in reaction, and the reaction will occur rapidly."
              }
            ],
            "id": "3jpzuu6sfki14i1",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The graph in the following activity shows the energy relationships for the reaction of a molecule of A with a molecule of B to form molecules of C and D:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "r2vq25pxrfeaysi",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "pndeto5odfiu8um",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "vidwjd5k2ppzx3o",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm A\\;+\\;\\mathrm B\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm C\\;+\\;\\mathrm D",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "2221850699",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
